  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/l168-zonancistrus-brachyurus/",
      "html": "<p>Zonancistrus brachyurus attains a maximum length of about 15 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/l168-zonancistrus-brachyurus/",
      "html": "<p>Zonancistrus brachyurus originates from the Rio Negro system in Brazil.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/l168-zonancistrus-brachyurus/",
      "html": "<p>L168 is very peaceful towards conspecifics and can be kept in larger groups.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/l168-zonancistrus-brachyurus/",
      "html": "<p>Keeping it in larger groups makes breeding attempts easier. Anyone trying to breed it is recommended to use very soft water with a pH of 5.5 to 6 and a water temperature between 26 and 28°C. L168 is a typical cave spawner.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/l168-zonancistrus-brachyurus/",
      "html": "<p>Due to several misidentifications this fish was initially sold in the hobby as Peckoltia pulcher, then Dekeyseria pulcher, sometimes also Zonancistrus pictus. The valid name (at least the current state of the art) is Zonancistrus brachyurus. In this case the L-number gives safer information than the scientific name. The species is often confused with the very similar L52 from the Orinoco basin.</p>"
    }
  ],
